{
 "title": "Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_M on gfx1151: decomposing a refused MTP due group into one-row cycles loses 19-26% per token even at perfect depth-3 acceptance",
 "date": "2026-09-18",
 "status": "measured_rejected",
 "performance_claim": false,
 "purpose": "Answer the mixed K/K0 question the concurrent-coverage review raised: when a due group is refused as a whole (static one-row evidence, a row that crosses the provider's 1023-token window, an unsupported target profile), should the engine serve each capable row on its own instead of decoding the whole batch autoregressively? Measured as three arms on two protocols at c=2 and c=4: AR control, whole-group AR (current default), and the one-row-cycle split (the route the adapter's partition contract closes).",
